    <bpmn:process id="W_W3460" name="W3460. Inverter / BESS Fault Management &amp; Vendor Warranty Resolution" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Inverter/BESS fault alarm (W3457); component failure
Frequency: Event-driven
Volume: ~1–5% inverter/year failure rate typical
Owner: Energy Manager
Participants: Energy Manager, O&amp;M, Vendor (manufacturer), Procurement (links to VS-03.3), Finance (links to VS-15)
Source: workflow W3460 — Inverter / BESS Fault Management &amp; Vendor Warranty Resolution</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3460_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3460_Lane1" name="Energy Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3460_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3460_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3460_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3460_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3460_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3460_Start3" name="Inverter/BESS fault alarm (W3457); component failure">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3460_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3460_Task4" name="Energy Manager/O&amp;M diagnose the inverter/BESS fault from SCADA logs and on-site…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Energy Manager/O&amp;M diagnose the inverter/BESS fault from SCADA logs and on-site inspection: error code, root cause (hardware, firmware, grid event), warranty status (W3453 serials), and impact; document the case
Responsible (R): Energy Manager / O&amp;M
Accountable (A): Energy Manager
Duration: Per event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3460_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3460_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3460_Task5" name="Energy Manager/Procurement engage the manufacturer/vendor for warranty…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Energy Manager/Procurement engage the manufacturer/vendor for warranty repair/replacement or out-of-warranty fix: RMA, lead time, cost, and authorization; manage a spare-inverter pool to minimize downtime
Responsible (R): Energy Manager / Procurement / Vendor
Accountable (A): Energy Manager
Duration: Per event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3460_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3460_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3460_Task6" name="Energy Manager restore the asset, validate performance recovery, capture the…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Energy Manager restore the asset, validate performance recovery, capture the fault/resolution in the asset history (links to VS-35), and feed recurring failures to procurement/quality (links to VS-31/VS-67) and reliability analytics (W3471); recover warranty cost (links to VS-15/W244)
Responsible (R): Energy Manager / Finance
Accountable (A): Energy Manager
Duration: Per event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3460_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3460_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W3460_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W3460_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
