    <bpmn:process id="W_W3464" name="W3464. Renewable Asset Safety, Structural &amp; Insurance Incident Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Safety incident; structural/equipment damage; extreme weather (links to VS-69)
Frequency: Event-driven
Volume: Event-driven
Owner: Energy Manager
Participants: Energy Manager, HSE (links to VS-24), Facilities (links to VS-20.3), Insurance (links to VS-26), Legal (links to VS-100)
Source: workflow W3464 — Renewable Asset Safety, Structural &amp; Insurance Incident Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3464_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3464_Lane1" name="Facilities">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3464_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3464_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W3464_Lane2" name="Energy Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3464_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3464_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3464_End8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3464_Start4" name="Safety incident; structural/equipment damage; extreme weather (links to VS-69)">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3464_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3464_Task5" name="On incident (module damage, fire, structural, electrical, fall, storm damage…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: On incident (module damage, fire, structural, electrical, fall, storm damage links to VS-69), Facilities/HSE secure the site, isolate the affected array, ensure personnel/public safety, and report per HSE (links to VS-24) and incident protocol (links to W330/W471)
Responsible (R): Facilities / HSE
Accountable (A): Energy Manager / Safety Mgr
Duration: Event-driven</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3464_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3464_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3464_Task6" name="Energy Manager/HSE investigate root cause (equipment defect, installation…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Energy Manager/HSE investigate root cause (equipment defect, installation, weather, maintenance), document, and remediate (repair/replacement via O&amp;M W3459 or warranty W3460); implement corrective action and feed to HSE/quality learning (links to VS-24/VS-31)
Responsible (R): Energy Manager / HSE
Accountable (A): Sustainability/ESG Manager
Duration: Event-driven</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3464_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3464_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3464_Task7" name="Energy Manager/Insurance file the insurance claim for covered damage (links to…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Energy Manager/Insurance file the insurance claim for covered damage (links to VS-26.3/W59 policy lifecycle/claims), recover cost, and update the asset record (links to VS-35); report material incidents to executives (links to VS-33.2) and audit/risk (links to VS-21.2)
Responsible (R): Energy Manager / Insurance / Finance
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: Event-driven</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3464_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3464_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W3464_End8" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W3464_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W3464_Annotation9">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-135 (ensure renewable asset registration &amp; net-metering settlement.) | - operational: protection, inspection, and HSE protocol; operational: structural design, insurance, and preparedness
Owner: Energy Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W3464_Assoc10" sourceRef="W3464_Annotation9" targetRef="W3464_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
